      "text": "To simplify the given expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\), we first need to find a common denominator. The denominator of each fraction is the same, so we can combine the fractions directly.\n\nThe expression can be written as:\n\\[\n\\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) + (3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, we simplify the numerator:\n\\[\n(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 + 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i + 25(-1) = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i.\n\\]\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5i + (5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i + 25(-1) = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n\\]\nAdding these two results together, we get:\n\\[\n-16 + 30i - 16 - 30i = -32.\n\\]\n\nNext, we simplify the denominator:\n\\[\n(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 - 25(-1) = 9 + 25 = 34.\n\\]\n\nSo the expression simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{-32}{34} = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}.\n\\]",
