      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to simplify the expression \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\).\n\nLet's break down the problem into manageable steps:\n\n1. Simplify each fraction separately.\n2. Add the simplified fractions together.\n\nFirst, we'll simplify \\(\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\). To do this, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} = \\frac{9 + 30i + 25i^2}{9 - 25i^2} = \\frac{9 + 30i - 25}{9 + 25} = \\frac{-16 + 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} + \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\nNext, we'll simplify \\(\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\) using the same process:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} \\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)} = \\frac{9 - 30i + 25i^2}{9 - 25i^2} = \\frac{9 - 30i - 25}{9 + 25} = \\frac{-16 - 30i}{34} = -\\frac{16}{34} - \\frac{30i}{34} = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\n\\]\n\nNow we can add the two simplified fractions:\n\n\\[\n\\left(-\\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17}\\right) + \\left(-\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17}\\right) = -\\frac{8}{17} - \\frac{8}{17} + \\frac{15i}{17} - \\frac{15i}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17} + \\frac{0i}{17} = -\\frac{16}{17}\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(-\\frac{16}{17}\\).\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the complex numbers\r\nnum1 = 3 + 5j\r\nden1 = 3 - 5j\r\nnum2 = 3 - 5j\r\nden2 = 3 + 5j\r\n\r\n# Simplify the fractions\r\nfrac1 = num1 / den1\r\nfrac2 = num2 / den2\r\n\r\n# Add the simplified fractions\r\nresult = frac1 + frac2\r\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n(-0.9411764705882354+0j)\n```\nThe result obtained from the Python code is \\(-0.9411764705882354 + 0i\\), which is equivalent to \\(-\\frac{16}{17}\\).\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}\n\\]",
